Subject: [PATCH] Collision evaluator: every owner-held checkout state guards,
 not only CLAIMED_INTEGRATION

On top of #3372. #3372 adds CLAIMED_INTEGRATION to the owner-held states, but
at main bb4f1ee five more ACTIVE shards omitted from the aggregate are still
unguarded:
- ELAN-INTR-BRIDGE-001 (CHECKED_OUT_CURRENT_SESSION; .github, StegVerse-SDK)
- ELAN-PUBLICATION-STRUCTURAL-CLARITY-001 (CLAIMED_IMPLEMENTATION)
- MYKV-HEALTHCARE-TRANSACTION-EVIDENCE-001 (CLAIMED_IMPLEMENTATION)
- SS-SKAP-ACCOUNT-INVENTORY-PROJECTION-001 (CLAIMED_IMPLEMENTATION)
- SS-SKAP-AUTHENTIC-ACCOUNT-METADATA-POPULATION-001 (CLAIMED_IMPLEMENTATION)

OWNER_HELD_CHECKOUT_STATES now covers CHECKED_OUT, CHECKED_OUT_CURRENT_SESSION
and every claimed member of scripts/cosv.py LIFECYCLE (CLAIMED_IMPLEMENTATION,
CLAIMED_VALIDATION, CLAIMED_INTEGRATION, MACHINE_OWNED). #3372's is_owner_held
gate is kept: apart from CHECKED_OUT, these states make a row eligible for a
hard collision only while coordination is ACTIVE-ish. Guards remain collision
evidence only; nothing is admitted or minted.

Refs StegVerse-Labs/.github#3372, #3369, #3195

